# WhereTo — environment
#
# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) and fill in. The app serves every page from the committed
# cache in data/cache/quotes.json, so it runs with no keys at all — the keys are only needed by
# `npm run warm`, which is the one thing allowed to spend them.

# Live prices. Free tier: 250 searches/month, 50/hour, no card. https://serpapi.com
SERPAPI_API_KEY=

# Destination content, generated at build time only. https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# The hard ceilings. Every paid call goes through lib/budget/guard.ts, which throws rather than
# degrading once the month's count reaches these. Deliberately under the provider's own limit, so
# a miscount cannot take the balance to zero.
SERPAPI_MONTHLY_MAX=200
ANTHROPIC_MONTHLY_MAX=800

# Optional, free: campground catalogue. https://www.recreation.gov/use-our-data
RIDB_API_KEY=

# Development only. Caches raw provider responses to disk so a dev-server restart, or a second
# warm run over the same matrix, does not spend quota again. Git-ignored, and separate from the
# committed cache in data/cache/ — raw responses carry account-tied URLs and have no business in
# the repository.
PRICING_CACHE_DIR=.pricing-cache

# Which SerpApi path the code takes. "fixture" (the default, and what you want almost
# always) reads recorded responses from fixtures/ and makes zero network calls. Only
# `npm run warm -- --live --limit N` sets this to "live", and it asks before spending.
SERPAPI_MODE=fixture

# Destination photography, fetched once at catalogue build by `npm run fetch-photos`.
# Demo tier is 50 requests an hour and needs no card.
# https://unsplash.com/oauth/applications, New Application, copy the Access Key.
UNSPLASH_ACCESS_KEY=

# Real road distances, fetched once at catalogue build by `npm run fetch-distances`.
# Free tier is 2,000 directions a day and needs no card.
# https://openrouteservice.org/dev/#/signup
OPENROUTESERVICE_API_KEY=
